Even if it wasn't intentional, it seems Robert Pattinson manifested his James Bond casting 14 years ago.

In 2012, during the height of his Twilight fame , the actor was asked in an interview with the U.K. online publication Shortlist if he could be playing 007 in 10 years' time.

&#8220;Yeah definitely,&#8221; he responded, &#8220;but more like 20 years.&#8221;

Pattinson added, &#8220;I think there'd be nothing worse than, like, &#x2018;Let's get a fresh-faced Bond!' That would be the worst idea in the world. After Daniel Craig, you have to have some baggage. It would be ridiculous to reinvent [him] as some young posh kid. Or, if [he] was, I'd have to get so tortured in the first few scenes. I'd have to do the first film with one arm or something." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Movies James Bond Found: Robert Pattinson to Play 007 Movies Matt Damon Reveals Ben Affleck's Review of 'The Odyssey' -- and the One Performance He Couldn't Stop Talking About

Around the time of the interview, the Primetime actor was preparing for the release of The Twilight Saga: Breaking Dawn &#8211; Part 2 later that year, and Craig was gearing up for the release of his third 007 movie, Skyfall .

In an earlier interview with BBC News in 2010, Pattinson also acknowledged that taking on cinema's most famous secret agent one day would be &#8220;quite big shoes to fill.&#8221; He also quipped that if he took over the role right then, he'd be &#8220;probably pretty bad.&#8221;

After 16 more years of acting experience and becoming one of Hollywood's most in-demand actors (Pattinson has starred in four films just this year alone), he clearly wasn't &#8220;bad&#8221; in his Bond audition. The Hollywood Reporter previously reported that Pattinson was among the finalists being considered for the role , in addition to Callum Turner, Jack Lowden, Josh O'Connor and Nicholas Hoult. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Director Denis Villeneuve and producers Amy Pascal and David Heyman ultimately decided Pattinson was perfect as the next 007 , taking over the iconic role from Craig, who concluded his run with 2021's No Time to Die .

" James Bond is one of the most legendary characters in cinema, and to be entrusted with 007 is the honor of a lifetime," Pattinson said in a statement about his casting. "I'm deeply grateful to Denis, Amy, David, Tanya and everyone at Amazon MGM Studios for their belief in me. To say this role is a dream come true is an understatement. I couldn't be more excited about this partnership and the work ahead with this fantastic team."

After a record-breaking summer, Sony Pictures is looking to soar even higher with its theatrical rerelease for Spider-Man: Brand New Day .

The studio announced Monday that the movie's extended cut will appropriately be titled Spider-Man: [Brand New] Brand New Day and is set to return exclusively to theaters on Friday, Dec. 4. The new footage will run 10 minutes in total and feature previously unseen scenes, including one with Rosario Dawson playing the Night Nurse. The rerelease will also include a couple of other surprises that have not yet been disclosed. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Movies Johnny Depp's 'Ebenezer' Unwraps $19M to Win Weekend in Box Office Return Movies Matt Damon Reveals Ben Affleck's Review of 'The Odyssey' -- and the One Performance He Couldn't Stop Talking About

Tom Holland made his big-screen return as Peter Parker in filmmaker Destin Daniel Cretton &#8216;s Spider-Man: Brand New Day , which was an absolute sensation upon hitting theaters July 31. It currently stands as the highest-grossing title ever at the domestic box office with $959 million, meaning that a rerelease could help push it beyond the billion-dollar mark for North America. Also starring Zendaya , Jon Bernthal, Mark Ruffalo and Sadie Sink , the movie ranks No. 3 on the all-time worldwide chart with $2.5 billion.

Also set for theatrical release on Dec. 4 are Universal's David Harbour-led sequel Violent Night 2 , the Pedro Pascal vehicle Behemoth! and Lionsgate's Idris Elba-starring action film Above the Below . Spider-Man: Brand New Day hails from producers Marvel Studios and Amy Pascal.

The Hollywood Reporter reported back in late September that Brand New Day would be returning to theaters with previously unseen footage. That news broke days after Marvel Studios' Avengers Endgame: Encore topped the weekend's domestic box office, with the rerelease of the 2019 box office smash grossing $26 million to prevail over a slew of newcomers. Endgame' s rerelease was timed to drum up additional excitement for Disney's Avengers: Doomsday , hitting theaters Dec. 18. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

During a fan event in July, Dawson told the crowd that she had filmed a scene for Brand New Day as Claire Temple &#x2014; the Marvel character she previously portrayed on the series Daredevil , Jessica Jones , Luke Cage , Iron Fist and The Defenders &#x2014; but that it landed on the cutting room floor.

&#8220;My character is somewhere in that same universe, and I really love that,&#8221; the actress said at the time about her character, who is a version of the Night Nurse. &#8220;I hope I get to be Claire again.&#8221;

While speaking with THR shortly after the release of Brand New Day , Sony film chief Tom Rothman addressed the challenge of following the studio's previous Spidey movie, 2021's Spider-Man: No Way Home , which featured the high-profile returns of previous Peter Parkers in Tobey Maguire and Andrew Garfield.

&#8220;The strategic decision was &#x2014; rather than trying what we all thought would be perhaps an empty effort of going quote, unquote bigger &#x2014; we just went deeper,&#8221; Rothman explained. &#8220;That was a very conscious choice to focus on how we could make the audience feel.&#8221;

Jonah, Saga, and a few allies in the police and FBI all suspect Jurek of having a disciple still operating in the outside world, who may know the location of a little girl who was also abducted. The launch into a bold two-front investigation, with Jonah hunting for the Jurek's acolyte and the missing victim on the outside, while Saga maneuvers to spy on Jurek and uncover anyone helping him by going undercover in the psychiatric facility where the killer has been locked away. But the deeper they get into the investigation, the more they're unsure if they're hunting Jurek, or he's actually the one hunting them .

I had the chance to speak with Nocturne showrunner John Hlavin at the press day for the show. I asked him about why he felt this was a series that needed to be added to the red-hot sub-genre of serial killer crime drama. According to Hlavin, it was a chance to create a very specific type of crime drama that American audiences may not be familiar with yet.

&#8220;So Rowan Joffe, who wrote the pilot, who was a British writer, and quite a good one, hooked up with me to make this into an American show, which he had very little experience doing,&#8221; Hlavin explained. &#8220;He had made TV before, but not an American show. I looked at it as an opportunity to take Scandinavian Noir, which I love, and truly adapt it for American TV, as opposed to replicating it into some, you know, almost Scandinavian version. You know, like as if we were to shoot it somewhere that looked like Sweden.&#8221;

Nocturne is indeed an imported show; the series is based on the mystery novel The Sandman by &#8220;Lars Kepler,&#8221; the pseudonym of the Swedish husband-wife writing team, Alexander Ahndoril and Alexandra Coelho Ahndoril. British author and screenwriter Rowan Joffe ( 28 Weeks Later, The American, The Informer ) then adapted that into this American TV concept.

Americans have limited exposure to Swedish crime-drama and Noir detective stories, with the most famous example being The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo book and movie series from late author Stieg Larsson; some fans were part of the wave of Swedish films based on the books, which became cult hits in 2009; others caught on when director David Fincher released his Hollywood version of The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo in 2011. Even though Fincher's film made money ($233 million at the box office) and won an Oscar and a Grammy, American audiences didn't seem to love it enough for Sony Pictures to invest in the rest of the series. A later reboot, The Girl in the Spider's Web (2018), was a massive failure, earning just $35.2 million at the box office and getting decimated by critics.

In short: Swedish Noir is a hard sell to Americans – at least in its native form. That's why Nocturne has made a key change to the genre: the setting. &#8220;I mean, that was the goal for me: how do we truly Americanize the story?&#8221; Hlavin said. &#8220;And then once Rowan and I settled on Western Pennsylvania, which is where we ended up filming it, I started to think about it through the lens of all the trees in Western Pennsylvania, and the way the light kind of moves through the trees and the rural communities and the separation of people.&#8221;And the fact that I'm from Ohio originally, the fact that, like, you know, people tend to keep to themselves. I sort of saw the overlap more clearly, and then it became something I was like, &#8216;Oh, this is an interesting way to tell this story, in a way that I haven't seen before.'&#8221;

&#8220;The first rule is always to entertain,&#8221; he concluded. &#8220;It's not an academic exercise. You're trying to find the most entertaining way, you know, to tell the story. And I think placing them in this location, in Western PA, in a way I hadn't seen Western PA shot before, at least not shot, in this way, was really the initial attraction for me.&#8221;

Nocturne streams exclusively on Apple TV.

